(EXP-47: comma-separated subjects test several variables against one value with
 `are`.
 Also covers: EXP-48 the `x, y, and z are true` shape, EXP-49 `are not false`,
 EXP-50 a single-quoted multi-word subject, EXP-52 subjects separated by
 commas, EXP-53 the `and` before the last subject being optional, EXP-54 the
 predicate applying to ALL subjects, EXP-55 `are not` negating for all of them.
 EXP-54 is the load-bearing one: the third block flips one subject and the
 clause must stop firing. EXP-55 likewise - with one subject still true the
 `are not true` clause must not fire, which is what tells a conjunction of
 negations apart from a negated conjunction.
 The last two lines record that the subject count is free: two and five both
 parse.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-47.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   all true
   none false
   and omitted, all true
   one flipped, no longer all true
   one of the three is true
   now all three not true
   two subjects parse
   five subjects parse
)
a boolean called armed is true.
a boolean called latched is true.
a boolean called sealed is true.
If armed, latched, and sealed are true then, Print "all true". Otherwise, Print "not all true".
If armed, latched, and sealed are not false then, Print "none false". Otherwise, Print "some false".
If armed, latched, sealed are true then, Print "and omitted, all true". Otherwise, Print "and omitted, not all true".
Set sealed to false.
If armed, latched, and sealed are true then, Print "still all true". Otherwise, Print "one flipped, no longer all true".
a boolean called 'door open' is false.
a boolean called lift_moving is false.
a boolean called lift_full is true.
If 'door open', lift_moving, and lift_full are not true then, Print "all three not true". Otherwise, Print "one of the three is true".
Set lift_full to false.
If 'door open', lift_moving, and lift_full are not true then, Print "now all three not true". Otherwise, Print "still one true".
If armed, and latched are true then, Print "two subjects parse". Otherwise, Print "two subjects false".
a boolean called warm is true.
a boolean called lit is true.
If armed, latched, warm, lit, and warm are true then, Print "five subjects parse". Otherwise, Print "five subjects false".
